---
title: "Card"
description: "Container that groups related content, with an optional header and footer."
tags: [layout, css]
usage: |
  Use an `<article>` with the `card` class. A `<header>` and `<footer>` inside it
  are styled as the card's header and footer.
accessibility: |
  - Start the card with a heading at the right level for its place on the page.
  - If the whole card should be clickable, keep a single real link (usually on
    the heading) rather than wrapping the card in one.
customProperties:
  "--card-border": "Border around the card."
  "--card-radius": "Corner radius."
  "--card-padding": "Inner spacing."
  "--card-gap": "Space between header, content and footer."
  "--card-header-font-weight": "Font weight of the header."
  "--card-footer-font-size": "Font size of the footer."
  "--card-footer-opacity": "Opacity of the footer text."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<article class="card">
  <header><h3>Card title</h3></header>
  <p>Card content goes here.</p>
  <footer><a href="#">Read more</a></footer>
</article>
